# ==========================================================================
# WMSHEET.ww2 -- THE RTCW SET'S WEAPON CARDS.
#
# What each gun IS. How its parts MOVE is WMCARD.ww2, the reload lane's, measured off the mesh.
#
# WHERE THESE NUMBERS COME FROM, and it is not one place. Full working and the evidence are in
# E:\DOOMWork\CardKit\sets\RTCW_NUMBERS.md; the short version:
#
# RealRTCW ships its own stats -- 89 .weap files in z_zzrealrtcw_scripts.pk3 -- so nothing here is
# invented. But ITS LADDER AND BRUTAL WOLFENSTEIN II'S DO NOT AGREE. Fifteen guns exist in both
# games and the ratio between them runs 2.67 to 6.67: the highest is two and a half times the
# lowest. No single multiplier carries one onto the other.
#
# The disagreement has a shape. SEVEN OF THE FIFTEEN LAND ON EXACTLY 10/3 -- every pistol, every
# SMG, the revolver. The two games agree completely about sidearms and submachine guns. What they
# disagree about is RIFLES: BWII flat-tops at 100, giving the Kar98k, Garand, BAR and Marksman
# Rifle all exactly the same number, while RealRTCW spreads that group across 15 to 35 and saves
# its highest for the scoped rifle. That is a real design difference between two games, not noise,
# and no arithmetic launders it away.
#
# SO: DAMAGE IS BY ARCHETYPE ONTO BWII'S LADDER, with 10/3 applied where the archetype agrees --
# which means every pistol and SMG below is just RealRTCW's own number times 10/3 and lands on a
# BWII tier by itself. CADENCE is BWII's for the archetype, scaled by RealRTCW's own nextShotTime
# ratio inside that archetype, so the Sten is a tic slower than the MP40 because RealRTCW says 115
# ms against 110 rather than because anyone guessed.
#
# A GUN IN BOTH SETS CARRIES THE SAME NUMBER IN BOTH. Eleven of these sixteen are also in the WW2
# set, and every one of them is identical here to its WMSHEET.bwolf entry. The sets never disagree
# about a gun they share.
#
# THE AMMO TYPES ARE OURS AND ARE A JUDGEMENT, not a reading. Every gun here feeds from Doom's
# Clip so Doom's own pickups feed the set.
#
# PROFILE NAMES ARE THE ww2_* ONES, because they are the same guns and those profiles exist.
#
# THIS SHEET ORIGINALLY NAMED rtcw_* PROFILES AND EVERY ONE OF THEM WAS DEAD -- 68 names under
# which nothing was ever built, so the set shipped firing with no flash, no smoke, no brass and
# no round look. Nothing caught it: card_lint checked sound names against SNDINFO and checked
# profile names against nothing at all. It does now. The lesson is the same one this project
# keeps relearning -- a name that resolves to nothing looks exactly like a name that works.
# ==========================================================================

gun "WW2_Luger"
  class
    slot               = 2
    selectionorder     = 9200
    ammo               = "Clip"
    hand               = main
    name               = "Luger P08"
    pickupmessage      = "Luger P08"
  end
  firesound            = "wm/m4a3/fire"
  # SHARED WITH WW2: identical to WMSHEET.bwolf's BW_Luger.
  # RealRTCW luger.weap 6 x 10/3 = 20 exactly. Cadence BWII's LugerP08, 6 tics.
  shotdamage           = 20, 20
  shotspread           = 1, 1
  firetics             = 6
  roundprofile         = "ww2_9mm"
  flashprofile         = "ww2_luger"
  recoilprofile        = "ww2_luger"
  ejectaprofile        = "ww2_luger"
end

